"""
## Purpose and audience
Boot-time NVMe lease contract for the OS VFS lane, written for the
storage/vfs owners. It pins how `os.services.vfs.vfs_boot_init` leases the
system FAT32 volume over NVMe, accepts production transfers from reversible
probes, assigns user-namespace leases to driver instances, and releases queue
owners on teardown.
## Operator workflow
Run `./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run test/01_unit/os/services/vfs/vfs_boot_nvme_lease_spec.spl`
from the repository root; scenarios build in-memory block devices and call the
boot init surface directly, so no NVMe hardware is required.
## Compatibility and limitations
The production-readiness, transfer-evidence, DBFS/NVFS, and standalone-q35
measurement scenarios assert shipped behavior that is currently RED (11 of 27
fail); they are kept RED deliberately to document the gap. Hardware-gated
coverage beyond the in-memory device model is out of scope here.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A red scenario means the boot-init surface diverged from the lease contract;
grep `src/os/.../vfs_boot_init` for the failing pinned token and re-read the
storage requirement before renaming either side. A load failure means the
`os.services.vfs` import root moved, not that the lease logic broke.
"""
